WEBVTT

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:20.500
You worry too much, Viktor. 
They only got away with a notebook.

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:24.000
That notebook has the 
combination to the safe in it!

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:35.130
What in the world?!

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:37.430
Did <i>you</i> do this?!

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:38.880
Hold it!

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:48.350
Nice work, rookie!

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:15.670
This place is as deserted as ever.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:18.600
The dictionary definition 
of the boondocks.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:19.360
Indeed.

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:23.500
You two noticed how all our jobs 
have gone off without a hitch lately?

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:25.860
Zenigata has not intervened.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:31.360
Exactly. And since persistence is the guy's 
middle name, it's starting to freak me out.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:34.880
Perhaps his continual inability to 
apprehend us has shaken his confidence,

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.650
and he has resigned from his position 
to wander the land as a ronin.

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:38.640
Nah. Not that guy.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:44.270
Well, he's been pursuing Lupin III, 
the greatest thief in the world, after all.

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:48.570
He should consider it an accomplishment 
that he's <i>almost</i> caught me as often as he has.

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:49.350
Right, guys?

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.320
Hey, don't all agree with me at once.

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:56.100
Wow. Real party town.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.000
We have been here before. 
Why have we returned?

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:03.240
Turns out, if you do a little digging, you can 
find plenty of loot ripe for the taking here.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:04.890
We might be in the middle of nowhere,

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:08.500
but this is where the Russian mob does 
its banking. Here, in the Yevgeny Bank.

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:14.000
The Krakenhaus is a jewelry chop shop where 
they "recycle" and sell on stolen wares.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:20.070
And the famous One-Winged Venus, an authentic 
piece from the time of the Colovini dynasty,

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:22.650
was "acquired" by a previous 
mayor as a spoil of war.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:31.270
<b>Zenigata, Gentleman Thief</b>

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:44.960
Would you look at that? 
Cops rushing to protect mafia money.

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:47.350
All right, off I go!

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:15.650
What?

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:20.960
We're under attack! 
Get in a car in the rear!

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:24.350
What the...

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:28.430
Give that back! Get back here!

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:45.950
Someone has spirited the 
target away before we could.

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:50.440
Whoa, what the heck? Did someone 
just swoop in and swipe our loot?

00:04:57.380 --> 00:05:00.410
Hey, watch it! It wasn't me! I wasn't involved!

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:02.200
Give it a rest, would you?!

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:04.440
You tryin' to kill me?!

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:07.200
Say what?

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.620
Zenigata was one of the thieves?

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:11.290
That explains everything.

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:13.210
The execution was like clockwork.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:16.420
I believe someone like Zenigata 
could manage such a feat,

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:18.900
as he has witnessed your 
methods time and time again.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:21.210
He has learned from your example, Lupin.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:25.970
Kinda sad that the master got 
"out-heisted" by the student.

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:30.890
Why would Zenigata be copying my act?

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:33.480
It's obvious, isn't it? It's some kinda trap.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:36.790
He pretends to be in the same line of work...

00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:39.240
and once our guard is down, 
he will attempt to apprehend us!

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:41.580
Did you just cut something?

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:44.480
Just don't go chopping the car in half, man.

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:45.600
You insult me.

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:48.480
Hey, the shutters are coming down.

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.790
All right-y. Off to work we go.

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:52.160
Hold it, Lupin.

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:54.210
Who are those men?

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:56.430
No way...

00:05:56.920 --> 00:06:03.000
Isn't the manager of Krakenhaus supposed to 
be off partying with his paramour right now?

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:05.510
Then, could these people be...

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:17.720
Nicely done.

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:28.020
Did you think copying me would 
throw me off or something?

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:30.600
Though, I admit, it did 
come as a bit of a surprise.

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:35.450
But I'm not gonna let you slap
the cuffs on me that easily.

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:40.050
Dammit! It was a trap!

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:40.870
Lupin!

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:54.900
Hey!

00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:57.630
We're trapped.

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:10.350
Sounds like the cops are on their way.

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:11.420
You're right.

00:07:16.130 --> 00:07:17.140
Come.

00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:20.480
That little... Okay, on to the next one!

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:25.570
He didn't even give Lupin a second 
glance. Just ran off with the loot.

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:26.670
<i>I see.</i>

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:29.740
Perhaps Zenigata truly 
has fallen from grace.

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:31.420
<i>"Fallen"?</i>

00:07:31.420 --> 00:07:34.430
Dismissed from the force
 due to his lack of results...

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:36.710
<i>...but with no other way of earning a living,</i>

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:39.830
<i>he could only think of using 
our methods to make money.</i>

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:42.690
So I'm his role model again? Gimme a break.

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:45.390
<i>I'm all set here.</i>

00:07:47.670 --> 00:07:48.690
<i>Let's do this!</i>

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:04.120
What's going on? A black out?

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:06.040
What's happened to the emergency power?

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:11.030
What was that?

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:14.790
Come to papa!

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:16.570
Huh?! What?!

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:19.350
What the...

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:31.430
They're making a run for it!

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:33.190
Get back here, you finks!

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:36.080
Uh, hi there, folks...

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:37.530
Stop!

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:38.940
Shoot him! Shoot him!

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:43.200
<i>Round up every police officer 
in town and hunt them down!</i>

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:57.740
Good thing there's all this snow around, huh?

00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:01.210
Hey, first-degree burns 
heal up in no time.

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:02.780
Seryoga!

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:03.490
Crud.

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:22.510
These people are not police, after all.

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:39.420
Hey, there!

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:40.670
You again?!

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:42.260
You're always so friendly.

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:45.260
You did a hell of a job back there, I'll admit.

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:49.010
What's got you pulling these 
kinds of heists, anyway?

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:52.540
Why would I tell a thief like you?

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:53.670
Is it the money?

00:09:53.670 --> 00:09:54.570
What?!

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:56.170
Doesn't sound like you, though.

00:09:56.170 --> 00:09:57.540
I don't need money!

00:09:57.540 --> 00:10:01.370
Oh, yeah? So what's the statue for?

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:04.280
I'm looking for something.

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:07.280
And I absolutely <i>have</i> to find it.

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:11.540
I get the feeling that each theft 
brings me closer to finding it.

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:15.810
Hey, thief! What's your name?

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:20.060
Shouldn't you be telling me yours first?

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:21.800
True enough.

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:25.440
But I don't know what my name is.

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:28.040
That's what I'm searching for.

00:10:28.650 --> 00:10:31.700
I need to learn who I really am.

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:34.060
Wait... you mean to tell me...

00:10:34.060 --> 00:10:37.580
Monety. That's the name I'm going by for now!

00:10:41.970 --> 00:10:43.240
We'll cross paths again!

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:20.750
You've really done it now!

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:21.750
Shut yer face!

00:11:24.020 --> 00:11:25.060
This guy...

00:11:25.880 --> 00:11:27.510
Hey, you okay, pal?

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:32.740
So you don't have a clue who you are?

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:36.930
Well, with no ID, there ain't 
much we can do about that.

00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:39.000
I chased someone here...

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:42.760
But they got away, 
so I was drowning my sorrows.

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:45.610
My head hurts. I can't 
remember anything else.

00:11:45.610 --> 00:11:48.150
You can crash here till yer memory returns.

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:50.330
But in exchange, you hafta 
come out on jobs with us.

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:51.400
Hey!

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:53.010
Jobs?

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:56.380
They're a little risky, 
but we <i>did</i> save yer life.

00:11:56.380 --> 00:11:58.380
So no complainin', y'hear?

00:11:58.380 --> 00:11:59.780
The name's Vacov.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:01.630
Oh well...

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:03.540
I'm Seryoga.

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:05.120
We're countin' on you, rookie.

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:18.670
That was amazin', man!

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:22.660
Yeah, man! You're a natural-born thief!

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:25.150
For some reason, I know a lot about thieving.

00:12:25.150 --> 00:12:27.380
It's about the only thing I remember.

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:29.980
You're just like this town.

00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:32.830
Yer head's full of snow right now.

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:35.900
When springs rolls around, 
everything will thaw.

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:41.190
When I'm stealing, I feel like 
I'm close to remembering who I am.

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:45.440
The bigger the job, 
the stronger the feeling gets.

00:12:47.310 --> 00:12:50.710
Well, we'd better set our 
sights on a bigger score, then.

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:57.710
Monety. We're gonna call you Monety.

00:12:57.710 --> 00:12:59.200
It means money.

00:12:59.650 --> 00:13:02.490
After all, that's what you're 
gonna be makin' fer us!

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:05.430
Money... Monety.

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:06.670
I like it!

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:10.210
I'm Monety!

00:13:13.210 --> 00:13:15.510
Vacov... Seryoga...

00:13:16.530 --> 00:13:18.910
Even on my own, I'm gonna keep at it.

00:13:18.910 --> 00:13:21.910
I need to pull off an even bigger heist.

00:13:22.970 --> 00:13:24.880
Otherwise, I...

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:29.480
I'll never remember who I am.

00:13:29.480 --> 00:13:32.990
<i>We've got a sale on second-hand vehicles! 
Get Japanese cars at an unbelievable price!</i>

00:13:32.990 --> 00:13:35.900
I figured it had to be something like that.

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:40.790
Returning to this remote town in 
the far north for a second time...

00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:47.500
Looking back, our last clash with Zenigata 
when he was a police officer was in this town.

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:52.260
And afterwards, our heists suddenly 
became a lot easier to pull off.

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:55.180
You came back here because you 
were worried about Zenigata.

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:57.840
Lupin, you old softy.

00:13:57.840 --> 00:14:00.020
It ain't like that, stupid.

00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:02.510
At least, not now, it's not.

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:05.320
What I'm worried about right now...

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:10.290
I mean, come on!

00:14:10.290 --> 00:14:16.030
That amateur managed to snatch 
the score out from under me! Twice!

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:19.290
Me! The greatest thief in the world!

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:22.050
It makes me sick! I'm so mad, 
I don't know what to do!

00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:26.540
He's using my own moves to upstage me!
 I mean, what the hell, man?!

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:31.530
It's a farce! Next time we run into 
that old bastard, he's really in for it!

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:33.430
What will we do next time?

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:35.840
Ain't it obvious?! Next time, 
we beat him to the punch!

00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:37.550
I'm gonna grab the loot before he can!

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:40.690
Looks like you'll get your 
opportunity soon enough.

00:14:41.830 --> 00:14:45.790
<i>The wealthiest man in town, Mr. Volhynia,</i>

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:49.450
<i>today received a calling card from the 
gentleman thief known as Monety.</i>

00:14:49.810 --> 00:14:51.870
<i>The card states the thief's intention</i>

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:56.410
<i>to steal the family's prized possession, 
the Eyes of the Romanovs,</i>

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:57.950
<i>and the police have been mobilized</i>

00:14:57.950 --> 00:15:01.840
<i>at Mr. Volhynia's request 
to ensure that they are kept safe.</i>

00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:00.970
Ha! He just keeps aiming higher and higher!

00:15:14.460 --> 00:15:18.970
Every officer in town is in position, sir. 
Security couldn't be tighter.

00:15:18.970 --> 00:15:20.170
I'm counting on you.

00:15:20.170 --> 00:15:22.480
My wife loves the Eyes of the Romanovs.

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:26.180
She says she can't sleep at night 
if she doesn't look at them first.

00:15:26.180 --> 00:15:27.220
Leave it to us, sir.

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:31.490
Beat some sense into this fool 
who calls himself a gentleman thief!

00:15:57.070 --> 00:15:58.260
I'm freezing!

00:15:59.010 --> 00:16:00.400
Don't catch a cold now!

00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:57.590
Dammit! After them!

00:16:57.590 --> 00:16:58.790
We can't!

00:17:01.810 --> 00:17:03.520
Our patrol cars are in pieces...

00:17:17.780 --> 00:17:19.970
I win, Lupin!

00:17:22.090 --> 00:17:24.190
What am I saying?

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:26.950
"Lupin"? Does that name sound familiar to you?

00:17:27.990 --> 00:17:32.770
Well... I <i>thought</i> it was the name 
of the greatest thief in the world,

00:17:32.770 --> 00:17:34.000
but now, I'm not so sure.

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:37.870
I feel so fulfilled!

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:40.490
You see?! I've beaten you!

00:17:41.360 --> 00:17:43.610
<i>Zenigata looks like he's on top of the world.</i>

00:17:44.060 --> 00:17:47.230
<i>Maybe he's actually happier like this.</i>

00:18:09.910 --> 00:18:13.400
<i>What... am I doing?</i>

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:16.210
You...

00:18:17.210 --> 00:18:19.780
Have we met before?

00:18:20.210 --> 00:18:23.070
It's a shame how things turned out, huh?

00:18:23.070 --> 00:18:27.550
What could we do? He wasn't 
gonna be workin' with us forever.

00:18:27.550 --> 00:18:29.610
Hey, look at this.

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:32.480
Why did they have <i>this </i>on them?

00:18:35.790 --> 00:18:38.770
The snow will melt, eventually...

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:42.780
I... I'm...

00:18:44.820 --> 00:18:47.800
Gone! They're gone! 
The Eyes of the Romanovs...

00:18:47.800 --> 00:18:50.550
You grabbed the right eye.

00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:54.320
And it's one of a set, you see.

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:55.450
What?!

00:18:56.110 --> 00:18:56.560
Huh?

00:19:00.650 --> 00:19:04.820
Looks like I win the final round of 
our little thieving contest! Yeah!

00:19:05.170 --> 00:19:06.220
This won't stop me!

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:08.490
I refuse to let you beat me!

00:19:10.180 --> 00:19:12.530
What <i>is</i> this feeling?

00:19:12.530 --> 00:19:14.820
For some reason, it's so familiar...

00:19:15.160 --> 00:19:17.100
See ya around!

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:35.120
Lupin!

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:40.280
We're here at Monety's hideout, the gentleman 
thief behind a recent spate of burglaries.

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:42.360
Two members of his gang have been arrested,

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:44.620
but Monety himself is still at large.

00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:50.860
Police suspect that Monety is in fact 
master thief, Lupin III, in disguise.

00:19:51.530 --> 00:19:54.380
The methodology of both
share a lot in common,

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:58.280
leading local police to reach 
out to Interpol for assistance.

00:19:58.830 --> 00:20:00.110
I'm embarrassed to admit this,

00:20:00.110 --> 00:20:02.890
but my memories of the 
last few weeks are a bit hazy.

00:20:02.890 --> 00:20:04.630
But rest assured!

00:20:04.980 --> 00:20:08.280
<i>As Interpol's primary investigator 
in all Lupin-related matters,</i>

00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:11.140
<i>he will </i>not<i> slip through my fingers again!</i>

00:20:11.470 --> 00:20:16.610
<i>I swear that I will do everything in my 
power to restore order to this town!</i>

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:22.410
<i>Just you wait, Lupin!</i>

00:20:26.090 --> 00:20:28.670
In the end, it actually got kinda lively.

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:31.170
Spring has arrived.

00:20:34.280 --> 00:20:38.480
<i>"Monety," huh? You were one hell of a thief.</i>

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:41.920
<i>After all, you stole all your 
plays from my playbook.</i>

00:22:16.090 --> 00:22:19.650
The global IT company, 
Shake Hands, is run by Enzo Bron.

00:22:19.650 --> 00:22:23.640
And now, the guy is using his new 
social networking service to hunt me down.

00:22:23.640 --> 00:22:25.350
It's called "PeopleLog."

00:22:25.350 --> 00:22:27.460
Somehow, this thing can 
tell you where someone is,

00:22:27.460 --> 00:22:30.720
and what they're about to do 
just from a single photo of their face.

00:22:30.720 --> 00:22:34.220
This time, it's not some game 
cooked up by a bunch of amateurs.

00:22:34.220 --> 00:22:37.990
If my disguises don't fool anyone 
anymore, what am I gonna do?

00:22:37.990 --> 00:22:40.470
Next time: An Outdated Master Thief.

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:45.000
<b>An Outdated Master Thief</b>

00:22:40.470 --> 00:22:43.070
Things are actually looking 
pretty hairy this time.
